{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Shalem.</b> Whole in his body — for he was healed from his limp; whole in his property — for he lacked nothing of all that gift; whole in his Torah — for he had not forgotten his learning in the house of Laban (Shabbat 33)." "<b>The city of Shechem.</b> Like 'to the city'; and similar to it: ״עַד בּוֹאָנָה בֵּית לֶחֶם״ (Ruth 1)." "<b>When he came from Paddan-aram.</b> Like a person who says to his fellow: So-and-so went out from between the teeth of lions and came whole — so too here: 'and he came whole from Paddan-aram' — from Laban and from Esau who encountered him on the way."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:58.746073506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}